|~ What is declared under `::keyword`: the refusal of its
   constructor, and the comparisons of keywords, which compare two
   keywords by their names in the one order. ~|

:keyword/construct |~~ Reads a keyword as itself. ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/PayloadNotKeywordError
  |~~ `::keyword` reads its payload as the keyword it is; a string
      becomes one by `keyword`.
      ~(
        ::keyword"k"
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::keyword/PayloadNotKeywordError ::string]
       )
  ~~|

:keyword/gt
  |~~ Whether the subject's name follows the name of the keyword the
      call gives.

      ~(:b | gt :a | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/gt/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:keyword/gt/than/NotKeywordError |~~ The than is a keyword. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::keyword)

:keyword/gt/greater |~~ Whether the subject comes after the value compared. ~~|
  ::boolean

:keyword/gte
  |~~ Whether the subject's name follows or equals the name of the
      keyword the call gives.

      ~(:b | gte :b | eq true)
      ~(:b | gte :a | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/gte/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:keyword/gte/than/NotKeywordError |~~ The than is a keyword. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::keyword)

:keyword/gte/atLeast |~~ Whether the subject comes after the value compared or equals it. ~~|
  ::boolean

:keyword/lt
  |~~ Whether the subject's name precedes the name of the keyword the
      call gives.

      ~(:a | lt :b | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/lt/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:keyword/lt/than/NotKeywordError |~~ The than is a keyword. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::keyword)

:keyword/lt/less |~~ Whether the subject comes before the value compared. ~~|
  ::boolean

:keyword/lte
  |~~ Whether the subject's name precedes or equals the name of the
      keyword the call gives.

      ~(:a | lte :a | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/lte/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:keyword/lte/than/NotKeywordError |~~ The than is a keyword. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::keyword)

:keyword/lte/atMost |~~ Whether the subject comes before the value compared or equals it. ~~|
  ::boolean

:keyword/keyword
  |~~ The name of the keyword, as a string: the reverse of `keyword` on
      a string, so `"foo" | keyword | keyword` answers `"foo"`.

      ~(:foo | keyword | eq "foo")
      ~(:"foo bar" | keyword | eq "foo bar")
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/keyword/text |~~ The name of the keyword, a string. ~~|
  ::string

:keyword/runLaws
  |~~ The results of the laws of the page of the binding the keyword
      names in its scope, one `{:law :says :actual :ok :error}` per law,
      `:says` the caption of the claim the law proves. A keyword after
      it runs the laws of the member the binding holds under it.

      ~(:limit |~~ Examples: ~(true) ~~| 10 | :limit | runLaws * /ok | eq [true])
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/runLaws/anchor |~~ The anchor within the page, null when it gives none. ~~| ~(at 0)

:keyword/runLaws/anchor/NotKeywordOrNullError |~~ The anchor is a keyword or null. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::keyword ::null)

:keyword/runLaws/results |~~ One result for each law: the law, its claim, what it answered and whether it held. ~~|
  ::vec
